data_needs:
NO NEW FEED, ROUTE, MODEL OR PAID DATA. Every input is already stored in events.sqlite, and every one is read only as stored before tau.

What R3-LEDGER and META-W read:
- the news table: headline, summary, source, knowable_at;
- filings.items;
- the first ok PROMPT-NEWS or PROMPT-DOC verdict answered before tau (score, guidance);
- news rows from the 72 hours before an event, for coverage;
- the six control streams' book.picks at tau;
- EVL-8's mrl_pool members and features: META-W depends on EVL-8's mrl.py, release 1019j or later;
- EVL-8's member outcomes, read only through its stored settled rows, forward-only, inside the state.

Births' facts use only those rows, under the SQLite authorizer. They never read bars, marks, outcomes, looks, bands, universe, meta, mrl_* or px.sqlite.

Calibration needs only the frozen synthetic generator and screen. No lane data was read by this design.

To verify after shipping (outcome-free counts):
- records accepted per night per stream;
- atom supply per recorded session;
- the window's awake/waiting/left counts against W_X;
- META-W's share of sessions with picks: about 1.5% expected under the null; a much higher rate is an alarm worth reading as a count.
